## Review Notes

- **No upstream visual baseline:** the upstream screenshots show "No data to display" in the chart body — that build drew nothing there. The card frame, legend, headline figures and follow-up pill remain valid references, but **the chart itself is built to spec** (static multi-series polyline, 2.25 stroke, optional grid, 24/22 padding). Do not pixel-compare the chart area against those two PNGs.
- **Why no chart library:** upstream uses `liveline`, which is React-only (`peerDependencies` lists react alone) and is switched into a fully static mode there (`paused`, `scrub={false}`, `pulse={false}`). Only that static slice is actually used, so it is implemented directly rather than pulled in as a dependency.
- **No area fill:** the one verifiable upstream call passes `fill={false}` and the other cannot be checked, so no `fill` prop is offered.
- Painting lives in `draw.ts` because jsdom returns `null` from `getContext('2d')`: kept inside the SFC it would be untestable.
